  "description": "<p>Currently, Direct and Indirect containers are created by providing RDF (as the original PUT/POST or via PATCH) that includes a triple of the form:<br/>\n&lt;&gt; a &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#DirectContainer\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#DirectContainer</a>&gt;</p>\n\n<p>That approach should be disallowed. </p>\n\n<p>Instead, the user should only be able to create a Direct container by POSTing or PUTing a new resource with a `Link` header as:<br/>\n``Link: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#DirectContainer\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#DirectContainer</a>&gt;; rel=\"type\"```</p>\n\n<p>Likewise, the user should only be able to create an Indirect container by POSTing or PUTing a new resource with a `Link` header as:<br/>\n``Link: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#IndirectContainer\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#IndirectContainer</a>&gt;; rel=\"type\"``` </p>\n\n<p>Note: Since Basic, Direct and Indirect containers do not inherit from one another, clients should not be able to change a container's type from one to another.<br/>\ne.g. Clients should not be able to change a Basic container to a Direct container.<br/>\nSee: <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/ldp/#fig-ldpc-types\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://www.w3.org/TR/ldp/#fig-ldpc-types</a></p>",
